@@ -163,6 +163,21 @@ Minecraft can't (a scripted scene, a web, a lever, a menu) or just to play Skyri
   with a Minecraft screen (inventory, chat) open.
 - It's keyboard-only for now, like the rest of SkyCraft's input.
 
+### Minecraft mobs in Skyrim's world
+
+Mobs you summon, spawn with an egg or release from a spawner live in Skyrim's world too:
+
+- They collide with Skyrim's ground and walls the way you do: they follow slopes and slide along
+  walls instead of climbing stair-steps. A mob outside the part of Skyrim's world that has loaded
+  stands still until it arrives, rather than falling out of the world.
+- Hostile mobs go after Skyrim's NPCs when no player is within their reach (zombies and spiders
+  walk at them, skeletons shoot them, creepers swell next to them). A player in reach still comes
+  first. NPCs take Skyrim damage scaled like your own hits, stagger from big ones, and bleed.
+  Nobody in Skyrim is blamed for it: no bounty, and no skill experience for you.
+- The NPCs don't fight back (a mob isn't something Skyrim's combat AI can see yet), and mobs that
+  run their own AI (piglins, wardens, endermen, the Ender Dragon, the Wither) don't pick NPC targets.
+- Add `-Dskycraft.mobsAttackNpcs=false` to Minecraft's JVM arguments to keep mobs off NPCs.
+
 ## Known limitations
 
 - If something goes wrong, `Documents\My Games\Skyrim Special Edition\SKSE\SkyCraft.log` says what.
